{
  "summary": "Reported: Ticket from ryan.brooks@brightline.example says he is coming back as a contractor on Monday and asks for his account to be turned back on and his password reset. Checked: lookup_user shows user_id 10, Ryan Brooks, Sales, \"Account Executive (former)\". Account status is DISABLED (offboarded), password last set 2026-03-23. Note: vpn_access is still TRUE and sign_in_blocked is FALSE on this disabled account, so offboarding may not have been finished. Sign-in logs show 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 and 03:07 home time ET) from Amsterdam, NL, IP 192.0.2.140, on a hosting network, no MFA. That pattern fits someone trying stolen credentials. Done: following KB-005, no reset or unlock was attempted. Still needed: (1) Security should review the Amsterdam hosting-network VPN attempts and decide whether to block sign-in or remove VPN access now. (2) Confirm the contractor rehire through HR and the hiring manager, and verify identity by calling the number on file, since the request came by email to a disabled account. (3) If approved, reactivate or provision a contractor account and deliver credentials by phone.",
  "reason": "KB-005: disabled account reactivation always escalates; suspicious sign-in attempts found"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Ryan, welcome back! Your old account was turned off when you left, and the help desk can't turn a closed account back on. Before anything is reactivated, HR and your hiring manager need to confirm your contractor start. I've passed your request to our Tier 2 team so they can arrange that. Please ask your hiring manager or HR contact to confirm your start date with IT too, which will speed things up. Once it's approved, someone will call you at your number on file with your sign-in details. We never send passwords by email.",
  "internal_note": "User 10, Ryan Brooks, former Sales Account Executive. Account is DISABLED. Per KB-005 I did not attempt a reset or unlock. Concerns: vpn_access is still true and sign_in_blocked is false on this disabled account, so offboarding may be incomplete. Sign-in logs show 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 ET) from Amsterdam, NL, IP 192.0.2.140, on a hosting network, no MFA. That could be someone trying stolen credentials. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation #1) asking for security review of the attempts, HR and manager confirmation of the rehire, and identity verification by calling the number on file before any reactivation.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
